{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multi-profile with avgpool clearly outperforms single-profile (config_002: 0.591 vs config_001: 0.485), and the best result so far is config_018 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc. However, aggregation method is completely untested beyond avgpool—transformer aggregation has never been evaluated. Question: Does transformer aggregation over profiles yield a meaningful improvement over simple average pooling in the strongest multimodal multi-profile setting? This is a single-variable change from config_018 (only avgpool→transformer), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why this is the best next experiment: Aggregation is the mechanism that determines how multi-profile information is combined, and since multi-profile was the single largest gain observed (~0.10 over single-profile), the aggregation strategy is a critical design axis with high uncertainty. If transformer helps, it unlocks a higher performance ceiling across many configurations; if it does not, we confirm avgpool sufficiency and can redirect budget toward encoder or fusion choices without wasting experiments on transformer variants."
}

